{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>The whole congregation.</b> They are the great ones of the land, who are the great ones of Israel. Some say: he curse his Elohim in secret. But the correct view is that the word Elohim is a name of attribute, and the angels are called Elohim, and likewise the judges. And who can know what is in the heart of the one who curses? But if he specifies the revered Name, which is not a name of attribute and is not combined with any name, for it stands alone — then the meaning is: at the time he curses, if he specifies the Name, he shall be put to death for pronouncing the Name, as the son of the Egyptian woman did. And for the honor of the Name, it is not mentioned explicitly. And it says <b>as the sojourner, as the native — he shall be put to death.</b> And it is possible that those quarrelers struck each other; therefore this section was written, though it was already mentioned. He only added \"as the sojourner, as the native it shall be,\" and began \"He who strikes any person's soul\" — intentionally, and not in war, whether sojourner or native."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:12.548780676Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}